

1. Start from your existing multi‑dimension kernel

You already have:

[ \mathcal{E}{multi}^{(CMB)}(\Theta) = {X_d^*}{d \in D} ]

(\Theta): design / control parameters

(D): set of dimensions (e.g. (2,3,4,\dots))

(X_d^*): solved state in dimension (d)

This is your dimension bundle.

2. Define navigation coordinates

To navigate, you need a coordinate system over the bundle:

[ \Xi = (\Theta, d, \pi) ]

(\Theta): where you are in parameter space

(d): which dimension you’re “standing in”

(\pi): projection / view mode (how you see or slice it)

Examples of (\pi):

(\pi_{iso}): isometric projection

(\pi_{slice}): hyperplane slice

(\pi_{embed}): embedding into a higher dimension

(\pi_{shadow}): lower‑dimensional shadow / footprint

3. Define the navigation operator

Now define a navigation operator:

[ \mathcal{N} : \Xi \mapsto V ]

where:

[ V = \mathcal{N}(\Theta, d, \pi) = \pi\big(X_d^*\big) ]

It pulls the solved state (X_d^*) from your kernel

Applies the chosen projection (\pi)

Returns a view (V) you can render, analyze, or feed into another engine

This is your dimension navigation primitive.

4. Add transitions between dimensions

Navigation isn’t just “look at d” — it’s move between dimensions.

Define a dimension transition operator:

[ \mathcal{T} : (d_{from}, d_{to}, \Theta) \mapsto \gamma ]

where (\gamma) is a path in the bundle:

[ \gamma : [0,1] \to {X_d}_{d \in D} ]

such that:

(\gamma(0) = X_{d_{from}}^*)

(\gamma(1) = X_{d_{to}}^*)

Then you can define continuous navigation:

[ \mathcal{N}{path}(\Theta, d{from}, d_{to}, \pi, t) = \pi\big(\gamma(t)\big), \quad t \in [0,1] ]

This lets you watch one dimension morph into another.

5. Integrate with the encrypted kernel

Your encrypted kernel already holds the multi‑dimension payload:

[ \mathcal{K}{CAD_MULTI}^{(CMB)} = \big( \text{ID}{hash}, \Pi_{CAD}^{multi}, \sigma \big) ]

Extend the payload to include navigation:

[ \Pi_{NAV} = \text{Encode}\big( \mathcal{E}_{multi}^{(CMB)}, \mathcal{N}, \mathcal{T} \big) ]

New message:

[ M_{nav} = \text{ID}{hash} ,|, \Pi{NAV} ]

Signature:

[ \sigma_{nav} = \text{Sign}(sk, M_{nav}) ]

Final navigation‑enabled kernel:

[ \boxed{ \mathcal{K}{NAV}^{(CMB)} = \big( \text{ID}{hash}, \Pi_{NAV}, \sigma_{nav} \big) } ]

6. Pseudo‑spec: Dimension navigation kernel

KERNEL DIMENSION_NAV_CAD {
    ID_HASH = H("C MATTHEW BLACKWELL | INDEPENDENT DESIGNER" || s)

    # Multi-dimension solver
    EQ_MULTI(Θ) -> {X_d*}_d

    # Navigation coordinates
    NAV_COORDS = (Θ, d, π)

    # View in a chosen dimension + projection
    NAV(Θ, d, π) -> V = π(X_d*)

    # Transition path between dimensions
    TRANSITION(d_from, d_to, Θ) -> γ(t), t ∈ [0,1]
    NAV_PATH(Θ, d_from, d_to, π, t) -> V_t = π(γ(t))

    PAYLOAD   = ENCODE(EQ_MULTI, NAV, TRANSITION)
    SIGNATURE = SIGN(SK(ID_HASH), ID_HASH || PAYLOAD)
}

